LICENSING OVERVIEW — "Moving Averages Follow Price" repository
==============================================================

This repository contains three kinds of material under three different licenses.
Read this header first; the full MIT license text (which governs the CODE) follows
below.

  1. THE MANUSCRIPT
     The paper manuscript under paper/ (the citable scientific record).
     License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0
     International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0).
     https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/
     You may share it with attribution, for non-commercial purposes, without
     modification. It is meant to be cited and quoted (within fair-use limits),
     not altered and redistributed.

  2. THE PLAIN-ENGLISH COMPANION
     The companion explainer under paper/ (filename ends in _companion).
     License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
     (CC BY-NC 4.0).
     https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
     You may share AND adapt it (translate it, excerpt it, build teaching
     materials from it) with attribution, for non-commercial purposes. The
     NoDerivatives restriction is deliberately NOT applied here, so the
     explainer can travel.

  3. THE CODE
     Everything in analysis/, data/pull.py, verify.py, the verification
     materials in verification/, claims.lock, requirements.txt, and other
     repository scaffolding.
     License: MIT License (full text below).
     You may use, copy, modify, and redistribute it freely with attribution.

For the avoidance of doubt: the verification and analysis code is released
permissively so that anyone can re-run and check the work. The raw price data
is not contained in this repository (it is exchange-licensed; see
data/SOURCES.md).

